## After rename — story-command amorce

For `bmad-build` and `bmad-code-review`, follow `.cursor/rules/bmad-story-context-amorce.mdc` for the first user-facing content (`Contexte de la Story`).

---

## Title formats

Use an em dash (`—`) after `BMad`. **Never append a date** (e.g. `(2026-06-19)`). The Agents sidebar already shows when each conversation occurred.

### A — Story ID compact (fixed shape, no topic, no colon)

These commands keep a compact ID-only title when a story ID is present:

| Skill / command | Title |
|---|---|
| `bmad-code-review` | `BMad — Code Review {Story ID}` |
| `bmad-build` | `BMad — Build {Story ID}` |

Omit `{Story ID}` only when none can be inferred. For `bmad-build` without a story ID, fall through to format B.

Examples:

- `/bmad-code-review 4-4` → `BMad — Code Review 4-4`
- `/bmad-build 8-4` → `BMad — Build 8-4`
- `/bmad-build` + story `8-4` in the message → `BMad — Build 8-4`

### B — All other BMad commands (label + short topic)

Also used for `bmad-build` **only when no story ID** can be inferred.

Format: `BMad — {Workflow Label} : {Topic}`

- Space before and after the colon.
- `{Workflow Label}` stays in English (command name).
- `{Topic}` is a short **French** subject (see Topic rules below).
- If no useful topic can be inferred (e.g. bare `/bmad-help`), use the label only: `BMad — Help` (no colon).

Examples:

- `/bmad-build` + disabled controls look (no story ID) → `BMad — Build : Look contrôles inactifs`
- `/bmad-correct-course` + bank unlock simplify → `BMad — Correct Course : Unlock banque`
- `/bmad-sprint-planning` → `BMad — Sprint Planning` (no topic needed)

